            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Rarely in the strictest sense, since most true commercial-duty machines use fixed frames for maximum rigidity. Some folding treadmills borrow commercial-grade components like stronger motors and reinforced decks without carrying a full commercial duty-cycle rating, offering a middle ground between home-tier and true commercial performance for buyers who also need to save space.",
