        <!-- SECTION 4 -->
        <h2 id="warranty" class="scroll-mt-24">
          Warranty Differences at the Commercial Tier
        </h2>
        <p>
          One of the clearest tells of genuine commercial-grade construction
          is the warranty a manufacturer is willing to put behind it. This
          isn't a minor detail buried in the fine print — it's the
          manufacturer publicly staking real money on how confident they are
          in their own build quality.
        </p>
        <p>
          Frame warranties at this tier commonly run 10 years or longer, and
          several of the machines in this roundup carry lifetime frame
          coverage, which is rare to see on home-tier treadmills outside the
          most premium models. Motor warranties are similarly extended,
          often five years or more on commercial-duty AC motors, compared to
          typical two- or three-year motor coverage on DC-motor home
          treadmills. Parts and labor coverage tends to be shorter across the
          board, usually one to three years, since that coverage reflects
          serviceable wear components rather than the core structural
          engineering the longer warranties are protecting.
        </p>
        <p>
          It's worth reading the fine print on commercial-tier warranties
          specifically around in-home versus commercial-use language. Some
          manufacturers offer a shorter warranty period if the machine is
          registered for a genuine commercial installation, like an actual
          gym or hotel, compared to a longer warranty period for the same
          hardware registered for residential use, since home use patterns
          are lighter even when the machine itself is commercial-duty rated.
          Always register your warranty accurately and keep documentation of
          your purchase, since commercial-tier repairs and replacement parts
          can be expensive out of pocket if a claim is denied on a
          technicality.
        </p>

        <div class="not-prose bg-amber-50 border border-amber-200 rounded-2xl p-6 my-8">
          <p class="font-black text-amber-900 mb-2 flex items-center gap-2">
