            <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">
              What actually makes a treadmill "commercial-grade"?
            </h3>
            <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
              A commercial-grade treadmill is built and warrantied for <strong
                >continuous, all-day use</strong
              > rather than a few hours per week. That typically means an AC
              drive motor instead of a DC motor, a duty-cycle rating for 24/7
              gym operation, a heavier fixed or reinforced frame, and a
              commercial-tier warranty from the manufacturer, not just
              marketing language calling a machine "commercial-quality."
            </p>
