          screen that rivals a boutique studio. The <strong class="text-white"
            >Life Fitness T3</strong
          > delivers nearly the same commercial-duty confidence for
          meaningfully less money, and the <strong class="text-white"
            >Precor TRM 243</strong
          > and <strong class="text-white">True Fitness M50</strong> each bring
          their own specialties, authentic gym-floor feel and best-in-class joint
          comfort, respectively.
        </p>
        <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
          For buyers who want commercial-grade performance without giving up
          floor space entirely, the <strong class="text-white"
            >NordicTrack Commercial 2950</strong
          > folds while still delivering serious hardware, and the
          <strong class="text-white">NordicTrack Commercial 1750</strong>
          remains the most accessible entry point into commercial-adjacent
          performance at roughly half the price of the least expensive true
          commercial machine here. Match your pick to how many hours a week
          the treadmill will actually run, not to the biggest number on the
          spec sheet.
        </p>
